BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the electrochemical potential equation for ion transport and explain how the Nernst equilibrium potential is derived.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Electrochemical Potential and Nernst Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Electrochemical Potential \(mu_bar\): For an ion with valence z across an electrical potential) Tj
T*
(   V_m:) Tj
T*
(   mu_bar = mu_0 + R*T*ln[C] + z*F*V, where F is the Faraday constant \(96,485 C/mol\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Free Energy Change for Inward Transport:) Tj
T*
(   Delta G_transport = mu_bar_in - mu_bar_out = R*T*ln\([C]in / [C]out\) + z*F*\(V_in - V_out\).) Tj
T*
(   Defining membrane potential V_m = V_in - V_out: Delta G = R*T*ln\([C]in / [C]out\) + z*F*V_m.) Tj
T*
(   3. Derivation of Nernst Potential:) Tj
T*
(   At thermodynamic equilibrium, net ion flux ceases, meaning Delta G = 0:) Tj
T*
(   0 = R*T*ln\([C]in / [C]out\) + z*F*V_eq) Tj
T*
(   z*F*V_eq = - R*T*ln\([C]in / [C]out\) = R*T*ln\([C]out / [C]in\)) Tj
T*
(   V_eq = \(R*T / \(z*F\)\) * ln\([C]out / [C]in\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Base-10 Transformation at 37 deg C \(310.15 K\):) Tj
T*
(   V_eq = \(2.3026 * 8.314 * 310.15 / \(z * 96,485\)\) * log10\([C]out / [C]in\) = \(0.0615 V / z\) *) Tj
T*
(   log10\([C]out / [C]in\) = \(61.5 mV / z\) * log10\([C]out / [C]in\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the enzymatic mechanism and structural cycle of the P-type Na+/K+ ATPase, detailing the E1 and E2 conformational states.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Na+/K+ ATPase is an electrogenic P-type primary active transport pump:) Tj
T*
(   1. Stoichiometry: Translocates 3 Na+ ions out of the cell and 2 K+ ions into the cell per) Tj
T*
(   molecule of ATP hydrolyzed, generating an outward net positive current.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Albers-Post Conformational Cycle:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1 \(E1 State\): The high-affinity cytoplasmic conformation binds 3 Na+ ions and 1 ATP) Tj
T*
(   molecule.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(Phosphorylation\): Terminal phosphate of ATP is transferred to a conserved aspartate) Tj
T*
(   residue \(Asp-369\) forming a high-energy acyl-phosphate intermediate: E1~P\(3Na+\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3 \(Conformational Transition E1-P -> E2-P\): Phosphorylation induces a major domain) Tj
T*
(   rearrangement, closing the cytoplasmic gate and opening the extracellular access channel.) Tj
T*
(   Concurrently, Na+ affinity drops ~100-fold, releasing 3 Na+ into the extracellular fluid.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4 \(K+ Binding to E2-P\): In the outward-facing E2-P state, high-affinity sites bind 2) Tj
T*
(   extracellular K+ ions, triggering dephosphorylation of Asp-369.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5 \(K+ Occlusion & Dephosphorylation\): Loss of inorganic phosphate yields the occluded) Tj
T*
(   E2\(2K+\) intermediate.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 6 \(ATP-Driven Return to E1\): Binding of a new ATP molecule to the low-affinity) Tj
T*
ET

