(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the Goldman-Hodgkin-Katz \(GHK\) voltage equation and how resting membrane potential is generated and maintained.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Goldman-Hodgkin-Katz \(GHK\) Voltage Equation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Statement:) Tj
T*
(   V_m = \(R*T / F\) * ln\( \(P_K*[K+]out + P_Na*[Na+]out + P_Cl*[Cl-]in\) / \(P_K*[K+]in + P_Na*[Na+]in) Tj
T*
(   + P_Cl*[Cl-]out\) \).) Tj
T*
(   Notice [Cl-] is inverted because its negative valence \(z = -1\) reverses the logarithmic) Tj
T*
(   quotient.) Tj
T*
(   2. Dominance of Potassium Permeability:) Tj
T*
(   In resting mammalian neurons and muscle cells, resting potassium leak channels \(K2P, Kir\) are) Tj
T*
(   open, giving a permeability ratio of P_K : P_Na : P_Cl approximately 1.0 : 0.04 : 0.45.) Tj
T*
(   Because P_K is 25 times greater than P_Na, the resting membrane potential V_m \(-70 mV to -80) Tj
T*
(   mV\) lies very close to the K+ equilibrium potential E_K \(-90 mV\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Role of Na+/K+ ATPase:) Tj
T*
(   - Direct Electrogenic Contribution: Pumping 3 Na+ out for every 2 K+ in contributes a small) Tj
T*
(   direct hyperpolarizing offset of -3 to -5 mV.) Tj
T*
(   - Indirect Maintenance of Concentration Gradients: The primary role of the pump is continuous) Tj
T*
(   maintenance of steep transmembrane concentration gradients of Na+ and K+, counteracting) Tj
T*
(   continuous dissipation via leak channels.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
