(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the molecular architecture of voltage-gated potassium channels \(Kv\) and explain their selectivity filter mechanism.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Molecular Architecture and Selectivity of Voltage-Gated Potassium Channels:) Tj
T*
(   1. Tetrameric Structure: Kv channels are homotetramers surrounding a central aqueous pore. Each) Tj
T*
(   subunit contains six transmembrane alpha-helices \(S1-S4 voltage-sensing domain, S5-P loop-S6) Tj
T*
(   pore domain\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Voltage Sensing: Helix S4 contains positively charged arginine or lysine residues at every) Tj
T*
(   third position. Membrane depolarization exerts an electrostatic outward force on S4, pulling) Tj
T*
(   the S4-S5 linker and mechanically dilating the internal S6 bundle crossing gate.) Tj
T*
(   3. Selectivity Filter Mechanism \(KcsA Paradigm\):) Tj
T*
(   - The filter contains the signature sequence Thr-Val-Gly-Tyr-Gly \(TVGYG\).) Tj
T*
(   - In aqueous solution, K+ has a hydration radius of 1.33 A surrounded by 8 water molecules.) Tj
T*
(   - As K+ enters the narrow filter \(3 A diameter\), dehydration occurs. The backbone carbonyl) Tj
T*
(   oxygen atoms of the TVGYG sequence mimic the octahedral hydration shell with precise atomic) Tj
T*
(   spacing \(2.8 A\), compensating exactly for the energetic cost of dehydration.) Tj
T*
(   - Why Na+ is Excluded: Na+ has a smaller ionic radius \(0.95 A\). It is too small to coordinate) Tj
T*
(   simultaneously with all 8 carbonyl oxygens without pore distortion. The energetic penalty of) Tj
T*
(   shedding its hydration shell is NOT compensated, preventing Na+ permeation by a factor of) Tj
T*
(   10,000:1.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
