(   1. Definition and Composition: Lipid rafts are dynamic nanoscale \(10-200 nm\), sterol- and) Tj
T*
(   sphingolipid-enriched microdomains within the plasma membrane. Sphingolipids have long,) Tj
T*
(   saturated acyl chains that pack tightly in a liquid-ordered \(Lo\) phase, segregated from the) Tj
T*
(   surrounding fluid liquid-disordered \(Ld\) glycerophospholipid matrix.) Tj
T*
(   2. Physicochemical Properties: Rafts are insoluble in cold non-ionic detergents \(e.g., 1%) Tj
T*
(   Triton X-100 at 4 deg C\), earning the operational definition Detergent-Resistant Membranes) Tj
T*
(   \(DRMs\). Cholesterol acts as molecular glue filling voids between bulky sphingolipid head) Tj
T*
(   groups.) Tj
