(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the nuclear pore complex \(NPC\) architecture and the molecular cycle of Ran-regulated nucleocytoplasmic transport.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Nuclear Pore Complex Architecture and Ran Molecular Cycle:) Tj
T*
(   1. NPC Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   The NPC is a massive 125 MDa multiprotein assembly with eightfold rotational symmetry spanning) Tj
T*
(   the nuclear envelope. It consists of nucleoporins \(Nups\) arranged in:) Tj
T*
(   - Cytoplasmic ring with 8 flexible cytoplasmic filaments.) Tj
T*
(   - Central scaffold/spoke complex embedded in the nuclear pore membrane.) Tj
T*
(   - Nuclear ring with 8 filaments converging into the nuclear basket.) Tj
T*
(   - Central channel filled with intrinsically disordered FG-Nups \(Phenylalanine-Glycine repeats\)) Tj
T*
(   creating a selective hydrophobic gel barrier.) Tj
T*
(   2. Ran GTPase Molecular Cycle:) Tj
T*
(   Directional transport depends on the steep gradient of Ran states:) Tj
T*
(   - High [Ran-GTP] inside the nucleus: RanGEF \(RCC1\) is chromatin-bound, loading GTP onto Ran.) Tj
T*
(   - High [Ran-GDP] in cytoplasm: RanGAP and RanBP1 localize to cytoplasmic filaments, triggering) Tj
T*
(   GTP hydrolysis.) Tj
T*
