(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the biophysical principles and experimental execution of the Patch-Clamp technique in measuring single ion channel activity.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Biophysical Principles and Configurations of Patch-Clamp:) Tj
T*
(   1. Principle: Developed by Erwin Neher and Bert Sakmann \(Nobel Prize 1991\), patch-clamp) Tj
T*
(   isolates a microscopic patch of cell membrane containing one or few channel proteins using a) Tj
T*
(   fire-polished glass micropipette \(tip diameter ~1 micron\) filled with electrolyte solution.) Tj
T*
(   2. Gigaseal Formation: Applying gentle suction creates an extremely tight mechanical seal) Tj
T*
(   between glass and membrane with electrical resistance exceeding 1 Giga-Ohm \(Gigaseal\). This) Tj
T*
(   eliminates background noise, enabling resolution of picoampere \(10^-12 A\) single-channel) Tj
T*
(   currents with microsecond temporal resolution.) Tj
T*
(   3. Four Recording Configurations:) Tj
T*
(   - Cell-Attached Mode: Pipette rests sealed on intact cell; records channels in native) Tj
T*
(   physiological state without disrupting cytoplasm.) Tj
T*
(   - Whole-Cell Mode: Strong suction pulse ruptures the membrane patch; pipette solution) Tj
T*
(   equilibrates with whole cytoplasm, recording macroscopic sum of all channels.) Tj
T*
(   - Inside-Out Patch: From cell-attached mode, pipette is rapidly withdrawn into air/bath; the) Tj
T*
(   cytoplasmic membrane face is exposed, ideal for studying intracellular second messengers \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   cAMP, Ca2+\).) Tj
T*
(   - Outside-Out Patch: From whole-cell mode, pipette is retracted so the membrane re-anneals with) Tj
T*
(   extracellular face outward; ideal for testing extracellular neurotransmitters and drugs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
