(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the structural basis of Clathrin-mediated endocytosis, detailing the roles of Clathrin triskelions, AP-2, and Dynamin.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Clathrin-Mediated Endocytosis \(CME\) Architecture and Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   1. Clathrin Triskelion Structure:) Tj
T*
(   The fundamental building block of the clathrin coat is a pinwheel-shaped triskelion consisting) Tj
T*
(   of three clathrin heavy chains \(190 kDa each\) and three light chains \(25 kDa each\) radiating) Tj
T*
(   from a central vertex. Triskelions self-assemble into a polyhedral geodesic cage composed of 12) Tj
T*
(   pentagons and variable hexagons.) Tj
T*
(   2. Adaptor Protein 2 \(AP-2\) Complex:) Tj
T*
(   Clathrin cannot bind lipids or cargo directly. The heterotetrameric AP-2 complex \(alpha,) Tj
T*
(   beta-2, mu-2, sigma-2 subunits\) functions as the molecular bridge:) Tj
T*
(   - Binds phosphatidylinositol-4,5-bisphosphate [PI\(4,5\)P2] on the inner plasma membrane leaflet.) Tj
T*
(   - Directly recognizes internalization motifs in cargo receptors \(e.g., YXXPhi motif via mu-2,) Tj
T*
(   or [DE]XXXL[LI] via beta-2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Recruits clathrin triskelions via its beta-2 hinge domain to nucleate lattice polymerization.) Tj
T*
(   3. Vesicle Invagination and Budding:) Tj
T*
(   Polymerization of clathrin forces the planar membrane to curve into a deeply invaginated) Tj
T*
(   clathrin-coated pit.) Tj
T*
(   4. Dynamin-Mediated Scission:) Tj
T*
(   Dynamin is a large GTPase that oligomerizes into a spiral collar around the narrow neck of the) Tj
T*
(   invaginated pit. GTP hydrolysis induces a concerted conformational twist and constriction that) Tj
T*
(   squeezes opposing leaflets together, severing the neck and releasing the vesicle.) Tj
T*
(   5. Uncoating:) Tj
T*
(   Immediately post-scission, Auxilin recruits Hsc70 chaperone, which hydrolyzes ATP to peel off) Tj
T*
(   the clathrin coat, recycling triskelions.) Tj
T*
