(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the structure and physiological role of Gap Junctions, explaining their gating mechanisms in cardiac synchronization.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Structure, Function, and Gating of Gap Junctions:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   Gap junctions are specialized intercellular channels providing direct hydrophilic cytoplasmic) Tj
T*
(   continuity between adjacent cells:) Tj
T*
(   - Six transmembrane connexin \(Cx\) subunits assemble into a hexameric ring with a central) Tj
T*
(   aqueous pore called a Connexon \(hemichannel\).) Tj
T*
(   - In the 2-4 nm extracellular gap, a connexon on one cell docks end-to-end with a matching) Tj
T*
(   connexon on the adjacent cell, forming a continuous 1.5-2.0 nm aqueous channel.) Tj
T*
(   2. Permeability Characteristics:) Tj
T*
(   Channels permit non-selective passive passage of inorganic ions \(Na+, K+, Ca2+\) and small) Tj
T*
(   hydrophilic metabolites up to ~1,000 Da \(cAMP, cGMP, IP3, ATP, glucose\), while retaining) Tj
T*
(   macromolecules \(proteins, nucleic acids\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Role in Cardiac Synchronization:) Tj
T*
(   In myocardium, Connexin-43 \(Cx43\) is concentrated at intercalated discs. Action potentials) Tj
T*
