(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the CFTR chloride channel, its domain architecture, gating by ATP, and how the Delta-F508 mutation causes Cystic Fibrosis.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   CFTR Architecture, Gating, and Pathogenesis of Cystic Fibrosis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Domain Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   CFTR \(Cystic Fibrosis Transmembrane Conductance Regulator\) is an atypical ABC transporter) Tj
T*
(   \(ABCC7\) that functions as an ATP-gated anion channel:) Tj
T*
(   - Two Transmembrane Domains \(TMD1, TMD2\): Form the chloride-selective pore.) Tj
T*
(   - Two Nucleotide-Binding Domains \(NBD1, NBD2\): Hydrolyze ATP.) Tj
T*
(   - Unique Regulatory \(R\) Domain: Rich in consensus protein kinase A \(PKA\) phosphorylation sites.) Tj
T*
(   2. Gating Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - Activation requires PKA phosphorylation of multiple serine residues on the R-domain.) Tj
T*
(   - Once phosphorylated, ATP binding at the two composite NBD interfaces induces NBD) Tj
T*
(   dimerization, which mechanically opens the TMD chloride pore.) Tj
T*
(   - ATP hydrolysis at NBD2 destabilizes the dimer, closing the gate.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Delta-F508 Mutation & Pathology:) Tj
T*
(   - The most prevalent mutation is a deletion of phenylalanine at position 508 \(Delta-F508\) in) Tj
T*
(   NBD1.) Tj
T*
(   - Delta-F508 does not completely destroy channel conduction; instead, it causes) Tj
T*
(   temperature-sensitive protein misfolding during synthesis in the rough ER.) Tj
T*
(   - Quality control machinery \(calnexin/Hsp70\) recognizes the misfolded protein, targets it for) Tj
T*
(   ER-Associated Degradation \(ERAD\) via the ubiquitin-proteasome pathway, and prevents it from) Tj
T*
(   reaching the apical plasma membrane.) Tj
T*
(   - In airway epithelia, absence of apical CFTR eliminates Cl- and HCO3- secretion,) Tj
T*
(   hyperactivates ENaC sodium absorption, and depletes the periciliary fluid layer, resulting in) Tj
T*
(   viscous dehydrated mucus, chronic bacterial infections, and respiratory failure.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
