(   3. Rotary Catalysis in F1:) Tj
T*
(   Rotation of the asymmetrical gamma shaft within the stationary \(alpha-beta\)3 head forces each) Tj
T*
(   beta catalytic subunit through three sequential conformations:) Tj
T*
(   - Open \(O\) Conformation: Very low substrate affinity; newly formed ATP dissociates, leaving the) Tj
T*
(   site empty.) Tj
T*
(   - Loose \(L\) Conformation: Binds ADP and inorganic phosphate \(Pi\) loosely; substrate cannot) Tj
T*
(   escape.) Tj
T*
(   - Tight \(T\) Conformation: Substrates are compressed together with catalytic residues,) Tj
T*
(   spontaneously synthesizing ATP without external energy input.) Tj
T*
