(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the biophysical mechanisms underlying Fluorescence Recovery After Photobleaching \(FRAP\) to quantify membrane diffusion coefficients.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Fluorescence Recovery After Photobleaching \(FRAP\) Theory and Execution:) Tj
T*
(   1. Experimental Methodology:) Tj
T*
(   - Membrane proteins or lipids are fluorescently tagged \(e.g., using GFP chimeras or fluorescent) Tj
T*
(   lipid analogs like DiI\).) Tj
T*
(   - A confocal laser beam focuses high-intensity illumination on a defined micro-region \(spot) Tj
T*
(   radius w, typically 1-2 microns\) for a few milliseconds, irreversibly destroying) Tj
T*
(   \(photobleaching\) fluorophores in that region without damaging the membrane.) Tj
T*
(   - Low-intensity laser illumination subsequently monitors recovery of fluorescence in the) Tj
T*
(   bleached zone over time as unbleached fluorescent molecules diffuse laterally into the spot) Tj
T*
(   from surrounding regions.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation of Diffusion Coefficient \(Axelrod Model\):) Tj
T*
(   - The recovery curve plots normalized fluorescence F\(t\) versus time t.) Tj
T*
(   - Half-time of recovery \(t_half\) is the time required for fluorescence to recover to 50% of its) Tj
T*
(   final plateau value \(F_inf\).) Tj
T*
(   - Lateral Diffusion Coefficient \(D\) is calculated as:) Tj
T*
(   D = \(gamma_D * w^2\) / \(4 * t_half\), where gamma_D is a beam-profile correction parameter) Tj
T*
(   \(approx 0.88 for circular Gaussian laser spot\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Mobile Fraction Determination:) Tj
T*
(   - Mobile Fraction \(M\) = \(F_inf - F_0\) / \(F_pre - F_0\) * 100%, where F_pre is pre-bleach) Tj
T*
(   intensity and F_0 is intensity immediately post-bleach.) Tj
T*
(   - If M < 100%, the remaining immobile fraction represents proteins tethered to the cortical) Tj
T*
(   actin cytoskeleton, extracellular matrix, or immobilized in lipid raft clusters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
