12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the biophysical properties of ionophores, contrasting mobile carriers \(Valinomycin\) with pore-forming channels \(Gramicidin A\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Ionophore Classification and Biophysical Mechanisms:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mobile Carrier Ionophores \(Example: Valinomycin\):) Tj
T*
(   - Structure: Cyclic depsipeptide containing alternating amino acids and hydroxy acids.) Tj
T*
(   - Mechanism: Has a hydrophobic exterior matching membrane lipids and a hydrophilic interior) Tj
T*
(   cavity lined with 6 carbonyl oxygens coordinating a dehydrated K+ ion.) Tj
T*
(   - Translocation: Binds K+ at one interface, diffuses across the hydrophobic core, and releases) Tj
T*
(   K+ at the opposite interface.) Tj
T*
(   - Temperature Sensitivity: Because transport requires physical diffusion of the carrier through) Tj
T*
(   lipids, carrier-mediated transport ceases abruptly below the membrane phase transition) Tj
T*
(   temperature \(Tm\) when lipids freeze into a solid gel state.) Tj
T*
