BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain how the Nernst-Planck electrodiffusion equation models ion flux across biological membranes.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Nernst-Planck Electrodiffusion Model:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fundamental Equation:) Tj
T*
(   The one-dimensional flux J_i \(moles / \(cm^2 * s\)\) of an ion species i across a membrane along) Tj
T*
(   the x-axis under simultaneous chemical and electrical gradients is described by:) Tj
T*
(   J_i = - D_i * \( d[C_i]/dx + \(z_i * F / \(R*T\)\) * [C_i] * \(dV/dx\) \),) Tj
T*
(   where:) Tj
T*
(   - D_i is the diffusion coefficient of the ion in the membrane.) Tj
T*
(   - d[C_i]/dx is the spatial concentration gradient \(Fick's diffusion component\).) Tj
T*
(   - dV/dx is the spatial electric field gradient \(electrophoretic drift component\).) Tj
T*
(   - z_i * F / \(R*T\) is the electric mobility related to diffusion via the Einstein-Smoluchowski) Tj
T*
(   relation.) Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation of Equilibrium \(Zero Flux\):) Tj
T*
(   Setting J_i = 0 yields:) Tj
T*
(   d[C_i]/dx = - \(z_i * F / \(R*T\)\) * [C_i] * \(dV/dx\)) Tj
T*
(   Separating variables: d[C_i] / [C_i] = - \(z_i * F / \(R*T\)\) * dV.) Tj
T*
(   Integrating across membrane thickness from x = 0 \(out\) to x = d \(in\):) Tj
T*
(   ln\([C_i]in / [C_i]out\) = - \(z_i * F / \(R*T\)\) * \(V_in - V_out\).) Tj
T*
(   Solving for V_m = V_in - V_out:) Tj
T*
(   V_m = \(R*T / \(z_i * F\)\) * ln\([C_i]out / [C_i]in\), which is precisely the Nernst equation!) Tj
T*
(   3. Constant Field Approximation \(Goldman Assumption\):) Tj
T*
(   Assuming electric field dV/dx = V_m / d is constant across the membrane allows analytical) Tj
T*
(   integration of the Nernst-Planck equation, directly yielding the GHK current and voltage) Tj
T*
(   equations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 26:) Tj
T*
ET
