T*
(   - Positioning of nuclear pore complexes.) Tj
T*
(   3. Laminopathies \(Hutchinson-Gilford Progeria Syndrome - HGPS\):) Tj
T*
(   - A de novo point mutation in LMNA \(c.1824C>T, p.Gly608Gly\) activates a cryptic splice donor) Tj
T*
(   site, deleting 50 amino acids near the C-terminus.) Tj
T*
(   - This removes the ZMPSTE24 cleavage site, resulting in a mutant protein called Progerin that) Tj
T*
(   remains permanently farnesylated and membrane-stuck.) Tj
T*
(   - Progerin accumulation disrupts lamina integrity, causes nuclear blebbing, loss of) Tj
T*
(   heterochromatin, telomere damage, and accelerated organismal aging.) Tj
T*
