(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the molecular mechanisms of primary cilia as cellular antennae and the role of intraflagellar transport \(IFT\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Primary Cilia Architecture, Signaling, and Intraflagellar Transport:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Organization:) Tj
T*
(   The primary cilium is a non-motile, solitary sensory antenna protruding from the apical surface) Tj
T*
(   of most mammalian cells:) Tj
T*
(   - Axoneme: Consists of an outer ring of 9 microtubule doublets lacking the central singlet pair) Tj
T*
(   \(9+0 arrangement\), without dynein arms.) Tj
T*
(   - Basal Body: Originates from the mother centriole docked at the plasma membrane.) Tj
T*
(   - Ciliary Transition Zone: Acts as a cytoplasmic gate with Y-shaped linkers restricting entry) Tj
T*
(   of proteins, establishing a specialized signaling microenvironment.) Tj
T*
(   2. Intraflagellar Transport \(IFT\):) Tj
T*
(   Because cilia lack protein translation machinery, all building blocks and signaling receptors) Tj
T*
(   must be transported along the axoneme:) Tj
T*
(   - Anterograde Transport \(Base to Tip\): Driven by heterotrimeric Kinesin-2 motor complexes) Tj
T*
(   hauling IFT-B trains along the axonemal B-tubule.) Tj
T*
(   - Retrograde Transport \(Tip to Base\): Driven by cytoplasmic Dynein-2 \(Dynein-1b\) complexes) Tj
T*
(   carrying IFT-A trains back to the cell body.) Tj
T*
(   3. Signaling Antenna Role:) Tj
T*
(   Houses critical developmental signaling pathways, notably Hedgehog \(Hh\) signaling: In the) Tj
T*
(   presence of Sonic Hedgehog \(Shh\), Patched-1 leaves the cilium, allowing Smoothened to) Tj
T*
(   accumulate, triggering Gli transcription factor activation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
