(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the structural mechanics of the bacterial flagellar motor as a rotary nanomachine driven by proton flux.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Bacterial Flagellar Motor Architecture and Proton-Driven Rotary Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   The bacterial flagellum is a rotary macromolecular machine spanning the cell envelope:) Tj
T*
(   - Filament: Long helical propeller made of flagellin subunits.) Tj
T*
(   - Hook: Universal flexible joint translating torque.) Tj
T*
(   - Basal Body \(Rotor\): Consists of the MS ring \(membrane/supramembrane\) and C ring \(cytoplasmic) Tj
T*
(   switch complex formed by FliM, FliN, and FliG\).) Tj
T*
(   - Stator Units: Non-rotating ring of 11-13 transmembrane MotA4-MotB2 protein complexes embedded) Tj
T*
(   in the peptidoglycan wall around the rotor.) Tj
T*
(   2. Torque Generation Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - Driven by the transmembrane Proton Motive Force \(pmf\) across the bacterial inner membrane.) Tj
T*
