(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the molecular composition of the Extracellular Matrix \(ECM\) and explain how Integrins mediate bidirectional inside-out and outside-in signaling.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Extracellular Matrix \(ECM\) Composition and Integrin Bidirectional Signaling:) Tj
T*
(   1. ECM Macromolecular Composition:) Tj
T*
(   - Fibrous Structural Proteins: Collagens \(provide tensile strength\) and Elastin \(provides) Tj
T*
(   elastic recoil\).) Tj
T*
(   - Specialized Glycoproteins: Fibronectin and Laminin containing Arg-Gly-Asp \(RGD\)) Tj
T*
(   integrin-binding motifs.) Tj
T*
(   - Proteoglycans & GAGs: Hyaluronan, heparan sulfate, chondroitin sulfate forming hydrated) Tj
T*
(   compressive gels.) Tj
T*
(   2. Integrin Heterodimers:) Tj
T*
(   Composed of non-covalently associated alpha and beta transmembrane subunits:) Tj
T*
(   - In the inactive bent state, extracellular headpieces have low ligand affinity, while) Tj
T*
(   cytoplasmic tails are clasped together.) Tj
T*
(   3. Bidirectional Signaling Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   - Inside-Out Signaling: Intracellular signaling cascades generate talin and kindlin, which bind) Tj
T*
(   the cytoplasmic NPXY motif of the beta-integrin tail. This disrupts the alpha-beta tail clasp,) Tj
T*
(   propagating an allosteric conformational extension up the stalks, opening the extracellular) Tj
T*
(   headpiece into a high-affinity ligand-binding state.) Tj
T*
(   - Outside-In Signaling: Extracellular ligand binding \(e.g., fibronectin RGD\) triggers integrin) Tj
T*
(   clustering, recruiting focal adhesion kinase \(FAK\), Src, and paxillin into focal adhesions. FAK) Tj
T*
(   auto-phosphorylation recruits Grb2-SOS, activating Ras-MAPK and Rho-GTPase cascades governing) Tj
T*
(   cell survival, motility, and differentiation.) Tj
T*
