(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the mechanism of Autophagy, detailing the molecular stages of autophagosome nucleation, elongation, and lysosomal clearance.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Molecular Stages and Regulation of Autophagy:) Tj
T*
(   1. Induction and Nucleation \(ULK1 and PI3K Complexes\):) Tj
T*
(   - Nutrient Starvation: Inactivates mTORC1 kinase, relieving inhibition of the ULK1 \(ATG1\)) Tj
T*
(   complex \(ULK1-ATG13-FIP200-ATG101\).) Tj
T*
(   - Class III PI3K Complex Activation: ULK1 phosphorylates Beclin-1 in the) Tj
T*
(   Beclin-1-VPS34-VPS15-ATG14 complex, generating localized phosphatidylinositol-3-phosphate) Tj
T*
(   [PI\(3\)P] on ER-derived omegasome membranes.) Tj
T*
(   2. Vesicle Elongation \(Two Ubiquitin-Like Conjugation Cascades\):) Tj
T*
(   - System 1 \(ATG12 Conjugation\): ATG7 \(E1-like\) and ATG10 \(E2-like\) covalently link ATG12 to) Tj
T*
(   ATG5. The ATG12-ATG5 conjugate binds ATG16L1 to form an oligomeric E3-like ligase.) Tj
T*
(   - System 2 \(LC3 Lipidation\): Pro-LC3 \(ATG8\) is cleaved by ATG4 cysteine protease to form) Tj
T*
(   soluble LC3-I. ATG7 \(E1\) and ATG3 \(E2\) transfer LC3-I to the ATG12-ATG5-ATG16L1 complex, which) Tj
T*
(   covalently conjugates phosphatidylethanolamine \(PE\) to LC3-I, forming membrane-anchored LC3-II.) Tj
T*
(   3. Autophagosome Completion and Cargo Capture:) Tj
T*
(   LC3-II lines both faces of the expanding phagophore, recruiting ubiquitinated cargo via adaptor) Tj
T*
